   "about": "Continuing register of correspondence and reports concerning movements of Japanese merchant vessels and related shipping intelligence.",
   "summary": "These pages continue a single file register, beginning with a sheet numbered 5 and running through a sheet numbered 46. Entries summarize telegrams, despatches, memoranda, and notes on Japanese ships’ port calls, routes, cargoes, bills of health, and tanker movements across the Pacific, Indian Ocean, and Americas. The register also records requests from the Navy and War Departments for movement reports and several related matters, including restrictions on ship supplies, suspected narcotics, and changing routes. Its entries range from December 1940 through July 1941.",
